      "p0001-n0012-l0007"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For Task2: We develop a hydrodynamic model tailored to the Great Lakes, account- ing for both the flow dynamics within the lake chain and external variables affecting it. Following this, we craft distinct water level control algorithms for the Compensating Works and the Moses-Saunders Dam. These algorithms integrate a mode-switchable feedback controller with a prediction module, enhancing the controller\u2019s responsive- ness by optimizing feedback gains for superior performance amidst environmental fluctuations. Simulations conducted using our model confirm the efficacy of these al- gorithms."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000017",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For Task 3: By increasing the outflow at the Soo Locks (upstream) and the Moses-"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000018",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "heading",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0004",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Saunders Dam (downstream), we evaluated their sensitivity to water level manage-"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000019",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0005"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0004",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0002",
      "p0001-n0013-l0003",
      "p0001-n0013-l0004",
      "p0001-n0013-l0005"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "ment. Our analysis reveals that the upstream dam predominantly affects Lake Supe- rior, Lake Michigan, Lake Huron, and Lake Erie, whereas the downstream dam has a more significant impact on the remaining lakes. When compared to water levels in 2017, our model demonstrates improved performance in numerous aspects."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000020",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0000",
